<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT -  Ralston buy reiterated.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT -  Ralston buy reiterated.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- SBC Warburg analyst Chris Jakubik said Thursday he &quot;strongly reiterated&quot; his buy rating on Ralston Purina Co, which makes Energizer batteries and pet food.</p>
<p>-- Jakubik said he took the action after Gillette Co and battery maker Duracell International Inc agreed to a $7.0 billion merger. Under that agreement, Duracell shareholders would receive 0.904 share of Gillette stock for each Duracell share owned.</p>
<p>-- Ralston shares were up 1-3/4 at 65-3/4.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
